=== TR [independent: (a)-(c) brute-force search over strategy profiles; (d)-(f) direct computation; (g) simulation; (h) identity] keys: signal, pausevalue, readiness, readrule (S11); the staying-out identity (X11)
    The transition: the signal game (separation, the bound on restraint after a reversible step, the intuitive criterion); a pause valued by what changes; readiness under conjunction and noise against sequential tests; staying out alone
(a) signal(1): a separating equilibrium (S sends, R does not, restraint after E only) exists iff kS <= GS and kR >= GR
  [ok] signal(1): brute-force search agrees with the condition in 300/300 random games
(b) signal(2): if 0 <= kR < GR and 1-mu < w, restraint after E has probability at most kR/GR in every equilibrium
  [ok] signal(2): over 200 random games, max over equilibria of (restraint after E) - kR/GR = 0.00e+00 <= 0
  [ok] signal(2): the hybrid equilibrium (S sends; R sends with prob (1-mu)(1-w)/(mu w); restraint after E w.p. kR/GR) is found in 135/135 games with kS <= GS kR/GR
(c) signal: the printed example
  [ok] kS=-0.05, kR=0.30, GS=0.40, GR=0.20 (mu=0.5, w=0.6): the separating equilibrium exists
   reversible step kR=0.05: separating exists: False; max restraint after E over equilibria 0.250 = kR/GR = 0.250; hybrid: R imitates w.p. 0.667
  [ok] kR=0.05: no separation; the step buys restraint with probability 0.25 at most
   pooling on N exists with skeptical off-path beliefs (restraint after E <= kS/GS): True; E is equilibrium-dominated for R (best -0.10 < 0) and not for S (best +0.30 > 0)
  [ok] intuitive criterion: beliefs after E must put weight on S, which removes the pooling equilibrium
(d) pausevalue(1): a pause that changes nothing leaves survival over any number of active rounds unchanged
  [ok] shift invariance in 200 random sequences
(e) pausevalue(2): hazard 0.01 a round for 20 rounds, then 0.01/k^1.5 in the k-th round after a change
   survival to round 10,000: 0.7969 (limit 0.7968); unchanged process at 0.01 a round: 2.25e-44
  [ok] survival to 10,000 rounds is 0.80 after a change to a summable sequence, 2e-44 without one
